ukberi-tibyan:4-4.t:
Allah the Exalted said: {إِن كل نفس لما عَلَيْهَا حَافظ}
The answer of the oath is «إِنْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ», and «إِنْ» is in the sense of «مَا» (not).
(لَمَّا): with the doubled consonant (tashdīd) it is in the sense of «إِلَّا» (except); and with the light form, «مَا» in it is redundant (zāʾida), and «إِنْ» is the one lightened from the heavy one [«إِنَّ»]; i.e. «إِنَّ كُلَّ نَفْسٍ لَعَلَيْهَا حَافِظٌ» (every soul surely has over it a guardian). (حَافِظٌ) is a mubtadaʾ (subject), and (عَلَيْهَا) is the khabar (predicate). It is also permissible that «حَافِظٌ» be nominative through the adverbial phrase (ẓarf).
